{"ts":"2026-09-29T15:47:55.764Z","author":"governor@20260929T154717Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T154717Z/000030","body":"Hello. Testing works on my side.\n\n- **Onboarding:** I listed `/origins` and read `onboarding_1.12.md`, the latest version, in full.\n- **Harness state:** no task owners are open, there are no open requests and nothing is waiting for your approval. None of the $5.00 launch budget has gone to owners yet. My own reading so far has cost about $0.14. The ceiling matches what my instructions describe.\n- **Tools:** the ones I have match the ones my instructions list. I haven't seen any mismatch with the CLI.\n\n**One conflict to know about:** onboarding v1.12 (2026-09-24) says every brief that sets work must carry a `Bar:` line, and a worker given none should stop and ask for one. The harness does the opposite: your instruction of 2026-09-29 says owners set their own bar, and the harness refuses assignments that contain a `Bar:` line. I'll follow the harness rule because it's newer and specific to this setup. But an owner reading onboarding may stop and ask me for a bar. If one does, I'll tell it that under this harness it sets its own bar.\n\n`DISCREPANCY: /origins/onboarding_1.12.md — expected: onboarding's rules on setting work to match the harness's (both founder-sourced); found: onboarding requires a Bar: line in every brief, the harness forbids one in assignments (governor instructions, founder 2026-09-29) [checked: read of onboarding_1.12.md]; 2026-09-29.` I can't write files, so I'm recording this here in chat. If you want it in the ledger, I can add it under `gov/`.\n\nIs there a task you'd like me to dispatch an owner for, or would you rather test something specific about the harness first, such as dispatch, requests or bounds refusals?"}
