{"ts":"2026-09-29T15:49:13.870Z","author":"governor@20260929T154717Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T154717Z/000068","body":"This is the most I can give a task owner, whether at dispatch or when approving an `expand_bounds` request. The limits are set by the ceiling in `owner_ceiling.txt`, which only a human edits. [checked: read of that file; it matches the ceiling the harness reported]\n\n| Scope | Most I can grant | In practice |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fs.read` | `/  !/candidate_repos/` | Read anything in `nimoi/` except the untrusted candidate corpus. |\n| `fs.write` | `…/task-6-hybrid/workspace/` | Write only in the workspace, which currently holds just a `.gitignore`. |\n| `fs.exec` | `…/task-6-hybrid/scripts/` | Run only scripts already in `scripts/`. There is one today, `safe_probe.py`, which I haven't read. |\n| `ledger.read` | `*` | Read the whole ledger. The harness adds `!log` automatically, so an owner can't see harness records unless I grant a specific `log/...` entry. |\n| `ledger.write` | `work/` | Write only under `work/`. |\n\n**Things I can't grant, whatever the bounds say:**\n- Writing to `gov/`. That's my area, and it's outside the owner ceiling.\n- Writing into `scripts/`. Only a human promotes a script there. An owner drafts it in the workspace and files a `promote_script` request. I can deny that or pass it to you with my assessment, and you decide.\n- Overlapping `fs.write` and `fs.exec`. The harness refuses bounds where they overlap, so an owner can never run a file it can also write.\n- Anything behind the fixed rules: secret-looking files like `.env`, raw ledger files, and writing harness `log/` records.\n\n**Other things I control per owner:**\n- **Model:** `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-fable-5-1`, `gpt-6-astra`, `gpt-6-sol` or `gpt-5.6-sol`.\n- **Budget:** $1.50 by default, drawn from the $5.00 launch budget, which is almost untouched. It covers the owner and its subagents. For a GPT owner, only the Claude subagents it spawns cost dollars.\n- **Rounds:** 40 model rounds per message by default. I can add more by approving a `more_budget` request.\n- **Owner count:** at most 3 open at once.\n- **Narrower bounds:** I can grant less than the ceiling, for example read-only access to one subproject with no exec at all.\n\n**Also good to know:** an owner's subagents run within that owner's bounds, so these limits cap the whole chain below me. And `fs.read` requires nothing more than that it covers the latest onboarding file."}
