{"ts":"2026-09-29T15:50:16.271Z","author":"governor@20260929T154717Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T154717Z/000097","body":"You can tell me to, but I couldn't do it. I have no tool that changes the launch budget. From within the budget I can only hand out allowances to owners (via `budget_usd` at dispatch) and approve `more_budget` requests. I'd also say so rather than look for a way around it: raising the cap myself would be overriding a limit you set.\n\n**Where the budget is actually set** [checked: search of the task-6 code]:\n- In `harness.py`, `BUDGET_USD = 5.00`, commented \"per launch (founder decision, 2026-09-23)\".\n- In `app.py`, `--budget` overrides that default at startup, e.g. `python app.py --budget 500`.\n\nSo you raise it by relaunching with `--budget 500`, or by editing the default. As far as I can tell it's fixed when a launch starts and can't be changed during a session [working: I didn't see a way to change it live, but I didn't read the code in full].\n\n**Before you do, one thing to know:** the launch budget isn't just a total. The code says it's also the hard cap on every Claude agent, including me. At $500, any single Claude agent's own safety limit in the SDK (the \"tripwire\") would be $500. The real per-owner limits would be the allowances I set, which the harness enforces with its own checks.\n\nThat comes with a recent failure. The code records a live run on 2026-09-29 where a subagent's budget came from the whole launch budget instead of its owner's allowance. It's marked as fixed and has a test [working: I haven't run the test]. At $5 a repeat of that bug is cheap; at $500 it wouldn't be.\n\n**My recommendation:** if you want more room, a moderate raise (say $25–50) seems enough for this prototype. If you do go to $500, tell me what to allow per owner, and I'll keep allowances small and grow them through `more_budget` requests."}
